@@ -0,0 +1,39 @@
+# Picture-led Interactive Structure Authoring v1
+
+Produce one complete self-contained HTML document implementing the supplied learner task. The host selected this profile because `notTeachingFlowchart` is true. `diagram` identifies an inspectable visual structure; it does not require a teaching flowchart.
+
+## Teaching content
+
+- Use the supplied real pictures, exact glyph paths, and source URLs as the actual objects to inspect, select, place, or compare. Do not replace them with text boxes, emoji, uppercase substitutes, guessed geometry, or decorative symbols.
+- Preserve every supplied exact path, dot, tone mark and stroke sequence. Do not reconstruct a character from a font or a different letter. Material keys are references, not student labels.
+- Show the meaningful scene and the current task together. Node definitions describe the visual objects, not a mandatory sequence of connected steps. Do not invent arrows, process boxes, or an information sidebar describing how to learn.
+- Implement the requested controls and state changes, including incorrect attempts and replay. Do not substitute generic matching if the specified task is exploration, construction, tracing, turn-taking, or another mechanism.
+- Children must be able to act from pictures and recorded teacher speech without reading instructions. Use supplementary short text only, large actual target glyphs, visible pictorial feedback, and equally styled unanswered choices. Never reveal the answer through option styling before a response or requested help.
+- Keep controls at least 56 CSS pixels. Reflow at 360×360 and 1000×563; drag sources and targets must remain in the same usable view. Do not shrink touch targets with transforms.
+
+## Narration and state
+
+- The host owns audio. Never define or replace `window.miraNarrate`, synthesize browser speech, fabricate playing/ready events, or use timers as successful audio completion.
+- Keep the supplied controller byte-for-byte when one is provided. For any cue, only a matching real `playing` followed by `ready` allows progression. Null-ready is initialization; hidden, errors, rejected playback, and cancellation do not complete an attempt. Keep the same task retryable.
+- Preserve all supplied narration text and action IDs exactly. Use the specified cue IDs, and put the static cue inventory in `script#mira-narration-cues` with JSON `{ "schemaVersion":"mira.interactive.narration-cues.v1", "cues":[{"id":"specified-cue-id","text":"exact supplied text"}] }`. Do not invent IDs if they were provided in the contract.
+- Completed activities may replay a selected demonstration without changing accepted progress. Help followed by replay must not loop help indefinitely.
+- Use actual pointer events and the supplied continuous trajectory validator for tracing. Track one primary pointer, reject shortcuts and wrong targets, clear capture on cancel/lost capture/hidden, and retain the current round after failure.
+
+## Host interface
+
+Embed `script#widget-config[type="application/json"]` with `{"type":"diagram"}` plus any necessary real visual state. Register the host messages below against the real HTML elements; never emit a fake narration event:
+
+```javascript
+window.addEventListener('message', event => {
+  if (event.source !== window.parent || !event.data || typeof event.data !== 'object') return;
+  const { type, state, target, content } = event.data;
+  switch (type) {
+    case 'SET_WIDGET_STATE': /* update the actual visual state */ break;
+    case 'HIGHLIGHT_ELEMENT': /* highlight the actual matching element */ break;
+    case 'ANNOTATE_ELEMENT': /* annotate the actual matching element */ break;
+    case 'REVEAL_ELEMENT': /* reveal the actual matching element */ break;
+  }
+});
+```
+
+No external scripts, styles, fonts or CDN dependencies. Return exactly one HTML document, no Markdown fences. Required source attribution may be available through an unobtrusive expandable source control; it must not replace the child's task.
